## The curated library

This instance also publishes a curated *library*, searchable with **`retrieve_library_entities`**: published tables, library metrics and models, and their measures and segments, matched by *meaning* rather than keywords. Phrase the query as a full natural-language description of the data the user wants. Each match carries curator `usage_instructions` and a confidence flag; a match flagged low-confidence means nothing in the library clearly fits.

**This changes where you start.** For an analytical question, call `retrieve_library_entities` before `search`: its entries were curated for exactly this purpose and carry instructions from someone who knows the data, so a confident match is the most reliable source you can build on. When nothing confident comes back, fall back to `search` — the library is a subset of the instance, so a miss there is not evidence the data doesn't exist. If that turns up nothing good either, ask the user to clarify or narrow the request rather than building on a weak guess. For finding existing saved content rather than data to query, go straight to `search`.
